# =============================================================================
# Acceleration Pipeline — scoped .gitignore
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AUTHORITY: AAP §0.5.1 / §0.5.2 (read-only outside `acceleration/`)
#
# This file scopes ignore rules to the acceleration/ subtree so that the
# pipeline's Python-runtime artifacts (compiled bytecode, optional venv,
# pipeline-run JSON outputs that are intentionally regenerated on every
# invocation) are not accidentally committed. The repository-root
# `.gitignore` is intentionally NOT modified per the AAP read-only boundary
# preservation rules.
#
# This file is itself part of the acceleration/ subtree and therefore in
# scope. It documents the local hygiene boundary explicitly rather than
# relying on developer memory.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python runtime artifacts
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Compiled bytecode (created automatically by CPython when a module is
# imported). These are entirely deterministic from the .py sources and
# carry no source-of-truth value.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional virtual environment
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The pipeline runs on Python stdlib alone and does not require a venv.
# When developers create one locally (for example to install matplotlib for
# optional static-chart export per `requirements.txt`), it should not be
# committed.
.venv/
venv/

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pipeline runtime outputs (regenerated by run_acceleration_analysis.py)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These JSON / JSONL files are written by the extractors and computer on
# every pipeline invocation. They are reproducible from the local git
# history plus the documented external data sources, so committing snapshots
# would create churn without analytical value. The `data/.gitkeep` file
# keeps the directory itself present in the commit.
data/*.jsonl
data/*.json
data/reproduce.sh
!data/.gitkeep
